-#
-# <use> clones live in a shadow tree that author CSS on this site CANNOT
-# reach. That constrains everything below:
-#
-#   - Element internals inside the symbol carry PRESENTATION ATTRIBUTES
-#     (fill="var(--tree-ink)"), not CSS rules. Convert them to CSS and the
-#     clubhouse collapses into one solid blob.
-#   - CUSTOM PROPERTIES are the only channel that crosses into the shadow
-#     tree. Per-instance control (--tree-ink, --house-wall, --window,
-#     --bulk, --lamp, --flicker) all goes through them.
-#   - Rules that must apply INSIDE the clone belong in the <style> INSIDE
-#     the <symbol>. The <style> OUTSIDE the symbol styles the light DOM
-#     only (it's how .scc-tree gets its aspect-ratio below).
-#   - --flicker MUST default to paused: inside the symbol it reads
-#     animation-play-state: var(--flicker,paused). A missing custom
-#     property must fail toward NO animation, or this becomes an
-#     accessibility regression nothing will flag.
-#   - Instances carry no viewBox of their own -- the symbol has it. Without
-#     the aspect-ratio:437/452 rule on the light-DOM .scc-tree class,
-#     instances collapse to 150px tall.
-#
-# Therefore: this markup was copied verbatim with a file operation, not
-# retyped. Do NOT reformat, "tidy", reindent, or minify it. Do NOT convert
-# presentation attributes to CSS. Do NOT move the inner <style> out of the
-# <symbol>. The ONLY deliberate change from the source is the light-DOM
-# class rename .tree -> .scc-tree on the outer <style> line (to avoid
-# colliding with unrelated classes elsewhere in Mastodon) -- everything
-# inside <symbol id="scc-tree"> is untouched, including id="scc-tree" and the
-# viewBox="-79 10 437 452".
